-- Import the corrected Hatch Batches workbook (394 rows), on your behalf.
--
-- Checked before writing, not after:
--   · 394 rows, every Setting and Hatch date a real date, hatch = setting + 21
--     days on ALL 394 (the day/month flips in the earlier file are fixed)
--   · settings run 05/09/2025 to 11/05/2026; flocks F-19 x 242, F-20 x 152
--   · all five hatchery names match Masters -> Hatcheries exactly, so every row
--     links to the master rather than sitting as loose text
--   · infertile + blasters + unhatched + hatched = setting on 393 of 394 rows
--     (row 366 is out by 2 -- left exactly as the sheet has it, not adjusted)
--   · hatch_batches was empty before this ran, so nothing can collide
--
-- Std Chicks = setting eggs x STD Hatch %, because STD Hatch % is the STANDARD
-- for that batch, not a count of chicks. It is therefore expected to sit ABOVE
-- the chicks that actually hatched whenever a batch fell short of standard --
-- that gap is the thing being measured, and Sale-STD reads it as a negative.
--
-- Culled Chicks is blank throughout the sheet, so it is stored as 0, and
-- Invoice No / DC No / Chicks Sold / Chick Rate / Remarks are blank as given.

INSERT INTO public.hatch_batches
